    "path": "java/sdk/pom.xml",
    "line": 620,
    "body": "`forkCount=0` disables the test JVM fork, so Surefire cannot apply this profile's `<environmentVariables>` (and the configured `argLine` is not applied either). As a result, `COPILOT_SDK_DEFAULT_CONNECTION=inprocess` never reaches the tests and the Surefire suite still exercises the default transport. This also contradicts the process-isolation requirement documented immediately above the profile; use one non-parallel fork.\n\nThis issue also appears on line 631 of the same file.",
    "subject_type": "line"
  },
  {
    "id": 3724184684,
    "path": "java/sdk/pom.xml",
    "line": 623,
    "body": "Once this variable reaches the forked JVM, unannotated direct-client tests still fail because the ambient InProcess connection conflicts with their legacy transport options. Examples include `ExecutorWiringTest#createOptionsWithExecutor` (`cliPath`, `cwd`, and `environment`), `MetadataApiTest`'s three CLI integration tests (`cliPath`), and `CopilotClientTest#testCliUrlAutoCorrectsUseStdio`, `testCliUrlOnlyConstruction`, `testTcpConnectionTokenAcceptedInTcpMode`, and `testCloseAfterFailedStart`. Adapt compatible tests to `E2ETestContext.createClient(...)` and annotate inherently subprocess-specific tests with a reason before enabling this suite-wide setting.",
    "subject_type": "line"
  },
  {
    "id": 3724184717,
    "path": "java/sdk/src/test/java/com/github/copilot/E2ETestContext.java",
    "line": 355,
    "body": "The guard remains active until the entire context closes, not until the client closes, so per-client environment overrides leak into later clients that reuse a class-level context. For example, after `RpcServerE2ETest#testShouldAddSecretFilterValues` sets `COPILOT_ENABLE_SECRET_FILTERING`, later guards do not unset that absent key; similarly the WebSocket experiment flag passed by `CopilotRequestHandlerE2ETest` persists for subsequent methods. Restore each client's overrides when that client closes (or otherwise reset them before the next client) to preserve the subprocess suite's environment isolation.\n\nThis issue also appears on line 369 of the same file.",
    "subject_type": "line"
  }
]

